\b FRST vs UNIFIED COHERENCE DYNAMICS - COMPARISON REPORT v1.0\b0\par
2026-09-11\par\par
\b Executive result\b0\par
Finite Relational Selection Theory (FRST) and Unified Coherence Dynamics (UCD) overlap strongly at the level of relational architecture, but they are not the same theory. FRST is a generic finite relational quantum architecture. UCD is a specific framework with Q72, H504 and H-net structure.\par\par
\b Common hierarchy\b0\par
\f1 mathematical possibility -> physical admissibility -> realized state/history -> observable reality\f0\par
Equivalently, Omega_realized is a subset of Omega_physical, which is a subset of Omega_mathematical.\par\par
A useful generic organization is (P_phys, H, rho_0): P_phys selects physically admissible states, H gives lawful dynamics, and rho_0 or an equivalent actualization law identifies the realized state/history.\par\par
\b FRST\b0\par
FRST v1.0 is summarized by R_FRST=(K,H_raw,P_phys,A_phys,H,rho_0,observables). It assumes a finite primitive carrier and treats geometry, fields, particles, mass, probability and classical records as effective or observable organizations of one constrained relational system.\par\par
\b UCD\b0\par
UCD is more specific. Its developed registration structure includes Q_72=Z_3 x Dic_6 and H_504=V_7 tensor C[Q_72], with dimension 504=7 x 72 and the developed 84+420 sector structure.\par\par
The finite H504/ring registration subsystem has exact gap Delta_504=2 kappa exp(-1/72). At kappa=0.1, Delta_504=0.19724142334878325. This is a finite UCD subsystem theorem. It is not automatically the continuum Yang-Mills mass gap and does not by itself prove global H-net finiteness.\par\par
\b Critical non-import rule\b0\par
FRST v1.0 assumes 0 < |V| = N < infinity. UCD must not receive this premise as a theorem. The UCD finite-realization program attempts to derive physical finiteness from its own upstream source law.\par\par
\b Completed creation and finite realization\b0\par
A completed set can be mathematically infinite. Therefore finished creation alone is not a cardinality proof. The UCD v14 work isolated a precise route: finite roots plus finite branching plus no infinite physically realized strict branch imply a finite realized tree by Koenig's infinity lemma.\par\par
The remaining UCD source obligations are P0-F1, finite immediate lawful actualization/finite branching, and P0-F2, no infinite physically realized strict differentiation chain/well-foundedness. The implication from those premises to finite realized tree is closed mathematics; the two premises remain source theorems to derive.\par\par
\b Selector theorem\b0\par
FRST makes the selector explicit as P_phys. A useful UCD organizational definition is H_UCD^phys=intersection_alpha ker(C_alpha) with P_UCD the orthogonal projector onto H_UCD^phys. This collects existing registration, gauge, holonomy, provenance and subsystem constraints under one operator umbrella, but does not prove that the selector has been uniquely derived.\par\par
The deeper target is a source theorem of the form Source law -> unique admissible selector -> Q72/H504/H-net architecture.\par\par
\b Machine progression\b0\par
v2 separated selector, actuality, finite realization and continuum-envelope questions.\par
v3 showed conditionally that finite alphabet plus bounded arity gives finite branching and a well-founded rank gives finite depth; symmetry alone does not generally select a unique theory.\par
v4 showed that finite Q72/H504 labels give a finite local codebook but do not prove global H-net finiteness.\par
v5 proved that a finite complete separating witness family is sufficient to bound distinguishable realized capacity.\par
v6 showed that such a separator family is an operational characterization of finiteness when arbitrary predicates are allowed, not the deeper cause of finiteness.\par\par
\b Continuum versus physical infinity\b0\par
The comparison distinguishes a finite physical ontology from an infinite or continuum mathematical envelope used for approximation and verification. A finite physical relational system may reproduce local continuum physics without asserting an actually infinite inventory of primitive physical registrations.\par\par
\b Current highest-value target\b0\par
The present foundational question is: what property of the UCD source law forces finite, well-founded actualization and simultaneously restricts the wider relational possibility space strongly enough to produce the specific UCD selector?\par\par
A successful chain would resemble Source/Law -> finite well-founded actualization -> physical selector -> Q72/H504/H-net -> observable physics.\par\par
\b Status boundary\b0\par
FRST v1.0 remains frozen independently. UCD remains the specific theory. The comparison is a theorem/countermodel program for exposing and testing missing derivations, not an automatic merger. Machine PASS results verify the encoded mathematical checks; they are not experimental validation of either theory.\par
